course: dictionary
lesson: 4397
title: Hairnets and hygiene
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are about jobs, and the sentence around them gives clues. «Food-factory workers wear hairnets, white coats and gloves» lists clothes that people wear to keep clean at work. Clothes worn for cleanliness are the first clue.
explain: The sentence goes on: «so no hair or germs get into the food.» That tells you what a hairnet is for. It holds hair in place so it cannot fall into food. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "a thin net worn over the hair to keep it out of the food" still makes sense.
explain: The second sentence uses the word again: «people in hairnets watched the machines». The clue is that the people are working in a factory, not hair. The meaning still fits: a thin net over their hair.
fact: A hairnet is a thin net worn over the hair.
fact: Hairnets keep hair in place, or stop hairs falling into food.
fact: «Hairnets» is the plural, and you can say «wear a hairnet».
fact: Hygiene means keeping things clean so that germs cannot spread.
fact: «Germs» are tiny living things that can make people ill.
exercise: «Food-factory workers wear hairnets, white coats and gloves.» Why do they wear hairnets? | To keep warm | To hide their faces | *To keep hair out of the food | To look fashionable
exercise: Find and copy the word for the thin net that workers wear. | samples | *hairnets | machines | chocolate
exercise: Ella says a hairnet is a big hat with feathers for a wedding. What is a hairnet really? | *A thin net worn over the hair to keep it in place | A pair of gloves for cooking | A hair clip for long hair | A large hat with feathers
test: «Dinner ladies wear hairnets when they serve lunch.» What is the main job of a hairnet here? | *Keeps hair from falling into the food | Keeps the head warm | Makes hair curly | Shows the person is in charge
test: A cook says, «Please wear a hairnet.» What does she want you to do? | Take off your coat | Sit down and rest | *Put a thin net over your hair | Wash your face
exam: Why do you think workers in hairnets wash their hands and walk through a shoe-cleaning bath? | To win a race | To play a game | To make their shoes shiny | *To keep germs and hair out of the food
